const COUNCIL = [
  { id: 'J1', name: 'Factory delivery judge', lens: 'long software tasks, spec-first, separated roles', scores: [5, 4, 6, 5], overall: 'The authority rule and role separation are right, but W2 as drawn could not certify a client deliverable: the read barrier was asserted while the repository documents it as absent, and nothing bound a certificate to the artefact it certified.', gaps: [['blocking', 'Read barrier asserted, not held: the verification README says "No read barrier" and a session-query tool can read the standard from the log.'], ['blocking', 'No durable substrate for a goal DAG: one goal per session, no ledger, no merge queue, no resume.'], ['major', 'Certificates were not bound to the artefact (no tree hash, no check hash) and departments as subagents could neither ask humans nor run their own preset.']], better: 'Certificate-first delivery: compile the signed spec into hidden per-goal standards plus one integration standard, run every goal as a fresh top-level session at host isolation, validate at each idle, certify the merged head, bind the release to a tree hash, and let humans attest the non-command outcomes.' },
  { id: 'J2', name: 'Sakana evolution judge', lens: 'Darwin Gödel Machine, ShinkaEvolve, evaluator hacking', scores: [5, 6, 5, 4], overall: 'A faithful map of the seams that stopped where evolution happens: choosing parents, identifying children, evaluating cheaply, and keeping the evaluator out of the mutator\'s reach.', gaps: [['blocking', 'No durable environment→session→seed record, so nothing in W1.4, W4.1, W3.2 or the held-out rule could be computed from the log.'], ['blocking', 'Component identity could not carry a mutation: a patched tool schema kept its parent\'s id, so lineage was unrecordable.'], ['blocking', 'Held-out verifiers were readable by the mutator through the tool-cordis façade.'], ['major', 'Best-only promotion labelled archive; the snapshot gate turned every prompt mutation into a re-record by the author.']], better: 'An archive-first harness DGM whose unit of evolution is a patch-layer bundle: variants are data that mount without a build, parents are sampled from an archive that keeps losers, a novelty gate and a staged ladder spend evaluation cheaply, and the PR exports a search result instead of being the search step.' },
  { id: 'J3', name: 'DeepSeek RL data judge', lens: 'RLVR at scale, reward hacking, training economics', scores: [6, 6, 4, 5], overall: 'A defensible rejection-sampling SFT design that was not yet an RL design; the scarce resource is a per-rollout, per-environment record with a tamper-proof reward, not GPUs.', gaps: [['blocking', 'No environment identity in the trajectory record: GRPO groups, decontamination and curriculum were impossible from the export.'], ['blocking', 'The reward was computable by the policy: checks ran in the implementer\'s workspace, so editing tests earned a certificate.'], ['major', 'Truncation was scored as failure, and exported messages were the post-compaction surface rather than any step\'s prompt.']], better: 'An environment-first, group-first factory: groups of eight rollouts per environment and policy version produced on demand, reward on a pristine fixture plus the patch with hidden checks, truncations masked, tokens joined by session, turn and step. Scenario A trains LoRA in the cloud for roughly 8 to 10 k€ per RL run; scenario B buys one HGX H200 node plus a rollout node and reaches one run every 3 to 4 days on-prem. Base family: GLM-4.5-Air first, pinned by pass@8 on the held-out suite.' },
  { id: 'J4', name: 'Hermes self-improvement judge', lens: 'skills as plugins, autonomy loops, self-modification safety', scores: [7, 6, 6, 4], overall: 'The spine is right; W4 claimed a provenance substrate the repository lacks and collapsed Hermes\'s two loops, refine in use and curate the core, into one PR pipeline.', gaps: [['blocking', 'Knowledge had no version identity in the log: skills, presets and compositions were name-only.'], ['blocking', 'Self-modification inside the loop could forge the reward: a dynamic package can append counterfeit verification data.'], ['major', 'No freeze between proposal and evaluation; the fast write-after-use tier was designed away; distilled client knowledge had no tenant scope.']], better: 'A two-speed loop over a content-addressed ledger: a fast loop where agents write and refine skills inside their department layer under a deterministic keep-or-retire board, and a slow loop where frozen experiments and a human move knowledge into the fleet; the observatory is a projection of the log, not a pipeline beside it.' },
  { id: 'J5', name: 'Determinism judge', lens: 'authority, replayability, invariants', scores: [6, 4, 5, 4], overall: 'The D labels outran the repository by three missing durable records (verification/run, environment/run, a budget block) and two semantic artefacts that had become oracles: re-recorded snapshots and synthesized checks.', gaps: [['blocking', 'Failed check runs left no durable record, so attempts and flakiness were unreplayable.'], ['blocking', 'Environment attribution was not logged; the run report was an in-memory value.'], ['major', 'Top-level structured output does not exist in the LLM seam; only the in-process subagent driver enforces a schema, through a scoped structured_output tool.']], better: 'Ten mechanically checkable invariants (certified ⇒ executed
